{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested for exact plan-publication candidate 61ccee16324dbf052771c57031492aa407f1e0ac under request #58.\n\n[PLAN-01] P1 — Separate P5 mirror-byte recovery from P6 decrypted projection recovery.\nEvidence: plans/001-confidential-application-prototype.md:430 declares P5 dependent only on P4 and G5. Lines 465–471 nevertheless require its test:relay/test:mirror completion to destroy local caches and recover the promised history, definitions and projection. The production retained folder and archive/client replay implementation arrive in P3 and P6; lines 475–478 explicitly say P6 integration needs P5. plans/README.md:18–19 prohibits proceeding past failed stage evidence, and lines 28–35 repeats the split dependency.\nExact source: https://github.com/generalbusiness-ai/noseq/blob/61ccee16324dbf052771c57031492aa407f1e0ac/plans/001-confidential-application-prototype.md#L465\nFailure scenario: an executor follows the declared order and reaches P5 with a working relay but no completed client replay/archive integration. It cannot supply P5's required projection recovery without implementing later-stage work, weakening the required evidence, or leaving both P5 and P6 incomplete. The statement that P6 pure/store tests may start early does not assign the full recovery acceptance case unambiguously.\nRequired correction: make P5 finish with independent retrieval and verification of retained signed/encrypted fixture bytes and all required artifact identities, with primary disabled and proof of no fallback. Assign full decryption, retained-definition loading and canonical projection/outcome recovery to P6 integration after P5, and compose the full A5 result in P9. Update the dependency diagram/index, command contracts and acceptance mapping wherever necessary so each stage can pass its own declared evidence using only completed dependencies. Do not add a reciprocal P5/P6 dependency or mark full replay passed on fixture byte retrieval alone.\nEffor